.Ss Fix: \(dqFile mode specification error: Cannot open load file … go-mode\(dq
.Ss Symptom
Opening Emacs (built from the remote branch) and visiting a
.Ql ".go"
file produced:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
File mode specification error: (file-missing Cannot open load file No such file or directory go-mode)
.Ed
.Ss Root cause
Both branches deliberately dropped the classic
.Ql "go-mode"
package in favour of the built-in
.Ql "go-ts-mode" ,
so nothing installs
.Ql "go-mode"
directly (it only ever arrives as a transitive dependency of
.Ql "gotest" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "go-tag" ).
But a
.Ql ".go"
file can still be routed to the classic
.Ql "go-mode" :
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
a \fBstale
.Ql "var/package-quickstart.el" Ns No "\fP"
carrying
.Ql "go-mode" Ns No "'s"
.Ql ";;;###autoload (add-to-list 'auto-mode-alist '(\(dq\e\e.go\e\e'\(dq . go-mode))"
after the elpa copy of
.Ql "go-mode"
was cleaned, or
.It
a \fBtreesit-auto grammar-missing fallback\fP, or
.It
an old
.Ql "auto-mode-alist"
entry.
.El
.Pp
.Ql "set-auto-mode"
then calls
.Ql "go-mode" ,
which
.Ql "require" Ns No "s"
a package that is not on
.Ql "load-path" ,
and the whole file-visit aborts with the mode-spec error.
.Ss Fix
Add
.Ql "major-mode-remap-alist"
entries in
.Ql "init-lang-go.el"
routing classic
.Ql "go-mode" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "go-mod-mode"
to their tree-sitter equivalents:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
(when (fboundp 'go-ts-mode)
  (dolist (remap '((go-mode         . go-ts-mode)
                   (go-dot-mod-mode . go-mod-ts-mode)
                   (go-mod-mode     . go-mod-ts-mode)))
    (add-to-list 'major-mode-remap-alist remap)))
.Ed
.Pp
.Ql "set-auto-mode"
consults
.Ql "major-mode-remap-alist"
\fIbefore\fP it loads the mode function, so
.Ql "go-mode"
is never required and every Go buffer lands in
.Ql "go-ts-mode"
regardless of how the file got routed.
In the full distribution the Go grammar is always present, so the remap resolves to a working
.Ql "go-ts-mode" ;
if the grammar were ever missing the failure would be a clear treesit-grammar error rather than a load error that breaks all file-visiting.
.Ss Fix: custom.el supersession prompt
.Ss Symptom
.Bd -literal -offset indent
custom.el changed on disk; really edit the buffer? (y, n, r or C-h) n
userlock--ask-user-about-supersession-threat: File changed on disk: ~/.config/emacs/var/custom.el
.Ed
.Ss Root cause
.Ql "custom-file"
is write-only
.No \&( Ns Ql "init.el" ):
the declarative config in git is the single source of truth, and
.Ql "custom.el"
is regenerated from scratch on every
.Ql "custom-save-all"
— which
.Ql "package.el"
triggers whenever it persists
.Ql "package-selected-packages"
after installing a package.
When more than one session writes it (a daemon and its
.Ql "emacsclient"
frames, or two Emacsen sharing
.Ql "var/" ),
the file changes on disk underneath the writer.
.Ql "custom-save-variables"
then modifies its buffer, Emacs notices the visited file changed on disk, and raises the supersession prompt (aborting the write with a
.Ql "file-supersession"
error if declined).
.Ss Fix
The file is disposable, so clobbering it is correct.
.Ql "init-core.el"
wraps
.Ql "custom-save-all"
so the supersession asker is a no-op during the save:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
(defun jotain-core--custom-save-without-supersession (orig &rest args)
  (let ((saved (symbol-function 'ask-user-about-supersession-threat)))
    (unwind-protect
        (progn
          (fset 'ask-user-about-supersession-threat #'ignore)
          (apply orig args))
      (fset 'ask-user-about-supersession-threat saved))))
(advice-add 'custom-save-all :around
            #'jotain-core--custom-save-without-supersession)
.Ed
.Ss Fix: go-mode crash recurs on every file; switch env from direnv to native devenv; tree-sitter cleanup
Three problems surfaced running
.Ql "just run-built"
and opening files.
The first \fIcompletes\fP the \(dqCannot open load file … go-mode\(dq entry above, whose
.Ql "major-mode-remap-alist"
fix turned out to be insufficient.
.Ss 1. Cannot open load file … go-mode on a Nix file (not just Go)
The earlier remap-only fix did not hold: opening a
.Ql ".nix"
file still raised the error and nix-mode never loaded.
Real root cause:
.Ql "go-tag" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "gotest"
drag in classic
.Ql "go-mode" ,
whose autoloads install a \fBglobal\fP
.Ql "magic-mode-alist"
entry
.Ql "(go--is-go-asm . go-asm-mode)" .
.Ql "magic-mode-alist"
is consulted for \fBevery\fP file
.Ql "set-auto-mode"
visits, and
.Ql "go--is-go-asm"
is autoloaded from
.Ql "go-mode" ,
so opening \fIany\fP file force-loads classic go-mode.
When go-mode isn't on
.Ql "load-path" ,
the load fails and mode setup aborts.
.Ql "major-mode-remap-alist"
does \fBnot\fP prevent this — it only rewrites the \fIchosen\fP mode; the magic predicate fires earlier and loads go-mode directly.
.Pp
Fix
.No \&( Ns Ql "init-lang-go.el" ):
strip go-mode's global autoload state at module load — remove the
.Ql "go--is-go-asm"
.Ql "magic-mode-alist"
entry and the classic
.Ql ".go" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "go.mod" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "go.work"
.Ql "auto-mode-alist"
entries (the module already routes those to the tree-sitter modes).
The remap stays as a backstop.
Verified in the built Emacs:
.Ql "flake.nix"
→
.Ql "go--is-go-asm"
gone, opens in
.Ql "nix-ts-mode" ;
.Ql ".go"
still opens in
.Ql "go-ts-mode" .
.Ss 2. gopls go: executable file not found in $PATH → disable direnv, use native devenv
.Ql "Direnv failed in .../otherproject/"
meant envrc applied no env, so gopls (global) couldn't find
.Ql "go" .
Trigger:
.Ql "just run-built"
launches Emacs \fIinside\fP jotain's own devenv shell (leaking
.Ql "DEVENV_*" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "NIX_*" ),
so envrc's nested
.Ql "use devenv"
for another project fails.
Decision: stop using direnv/envrc; load the environment natively via devenv.
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Ql "devenv.el" :
new
.Ql "devenv-env-defer-to-direnv"
defcustom (default
.Ql "t" ,
keeps the library reusable);
.Ql "devenv-env--turn-on"
only skips
.Ql ".envrc" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "envrc-mode"
buffers when it is non-nil.
New
.Ql "devenv-env-loading-p"
predicate reports an in-flight
.Ql "print-dev-env"
fetch.
.It
.Ql "init-prog.el" :
removed the
.Ql "envrc"
.Ql "use-package"
block; removed the curated per-mode
.Ql ":hook . eglot-ensure"
(it fired \fIbefore\fP the globalized
.Ql "devenv-env-mode"
turned on, so eglot connected with the global env).
Hardened
.Ql "jotain-prog--maybe-eglot-ensure"
to call
.Ql "eglot-ensure"
unconditionally while the devenv env is loading (the loader's deferral advice holds and replays it once the env lands), keeping the
.Ql "executable-find"
guard only for the settled path.
.It
.Ql "init-devenv.el" :
enable
.Ql "devenv-env-global-mode"
on
.Ql "after-init" ,
set
.Ql "devenv-env-defer-to-direnv"
nil.
.El
.Pp
Trust:
.Ql "devenv-env-mode"
only activates for projects trusted with
.Ql "devenv-allow"
.No \&( Ns Ql "C-c v" );
until then the mode line shows
.Ql "devenv[!]" .
Trade-off: pure-direnv, non-devenv projects lose auto-env.
Verified: the loader enables cleanly and installs the
.Ql "eglot-ensure"
deferral advice.
(Interactive confirmation that gopls finds
.Ql "go"
in otherproject, and whether otherproject is a devenv project, is the remaining user step.)
.Ss 3. Tree-sitter cleanup
The
.Ql "TREE_SITTER_DIR"
→
.Ql "treesit-extra-load-path"
block in
.Ql "early-init.el"
was dead: nothing set that env var.
Grammars come from Nixpkgs' own
.Ql "site-start.el"
.No \&( Ns Ql "treesit-extra-load-path"
→
.Ql "…/emacs-packages-deps/lib/" ).
Removed the block, fixed the stale comment in
.Ql "init-prog.el" ,
and stopped the async native-comp \(dqgrammar for go unavailable\(dq warning by propagating the path into workers (which run without site files):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
(setq native-comp-async-env-modifier-form
      `(setq treesit-extra-load-path ',treesit-extra-load-path))
.Ed
.Ss Note: stale lisp/.elc shadow source edits
.Ql "early-init.el"
sets
.Ql "load-prefer-newer"
to
.Ql "noninteractive" ,
so an \fIinteractive\fP Emacs prefers
.Ql ".elc"
even when the
.Ql ".el"
is newer.
A prior
.Ql "just compile"
had left stale
.Ql "lisp/*.elc"
(devenv, init-devenv, init-lang-go, …) that would shadow these edits.
Ran
.Ql "just clean"
to clear them and the eln-cache; the next
.Ql "just run-built"
recompiles from source.
.Ql "nix flake check" Ns No "'s"
elisp-compile (warnings-as-errors) passes with the edits.
.Ss Drop treesit-auto; route tree-sitter modes ourselves
.Ql "treesit-auto"
was already running with both of its headline features off:
.Ql "treesit-auto-install nil"
(Nix provides every grammar) and
.Ql "global-treesit-auto-mode"
deliberately unused (it advises
.Ql "set-auto-mode-0"
and cost ~3.6 s per
.Ql "find-file" ).
All it still did was
.Ql "(treesit-auto-add-to-auto-mode-alist 'all)"
for the long tail and supply the recipe list behind
.Ql "jotain-prog--warn-non-ts-mode" .
Meanwhile every
.Ql "init-lang-*.el"
already routed its language explicitly, so routing was split-brain and the diagnostic reached into the package's struct accessors.
.Pp
Emacs ships no built-in lang→regex table, so \fIsome\fP table is unavoidable; owning a small one beats depending on a community recipe list.
.Ss Change
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Ql "init-prog.el" :
removed the
.Ql "treesit-auto"
.Ql "use-package"
block; added
.Ql "jotain-prog-ts-remaps"
(entries
.Ql "(LANG TS-MODE CLASSIC-MODE...)" )
and
.Ql "jotain-prog--apply-ts-remaps" ,
a
.Ql "treesit-ready-p" Ns No "-guarded"
loop that populates
.Ql "major-mode-remap-alist" .
Remapping the \fIchosen\fP mode means we own no file regexes: each classic mode's own autoload stays the source of truth and we just redirect it.
Same mechanism
.Ql "init-lang-go.el"
uses.
.It
Expanded coverage to silence the diagnostic:
.Ql "sh-mode" Ns No "→" Ns Ql "bash-ts-mode" ,
.Ql "cmake-mode" Ns No "→" Ns Ql "cmake-ts-mode" ,
.Ql "dockerfile-mode" Ns No "→" Ns Ql "dockerfile-ts-mode" ,
.Ql "js-json-mode" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "json-mode" Ns No "→" Ns Ql "json-ts-mode" ,
.Ql "conf-toml-mode" Ns No "→"
.Ql "toml-ts-mode" ,
.Ql "yaml-mode" Ns No "→" Ns Ql "yaml-ts-mode"
(plus python/rust/css/js/ts belt-and-suspenders).
.It
Rewrote
.Ql "jotain-prog--warn-non-ts-mode"
to be self-contained: it derives
.Ql "foo-ts-mode" Ns No "/grammar"
from the mode name instead of reading
.Ql "treesit-auto-recipe-list" .
It's now a gap detector for \fIunrouted\fP languages (routed ones never reach it).
.It
.Ql "dockerfile"
eglot server keyed on
.Ql "(dockerfile-ts-mode dockerfile-mode)"
so
.Ql "docker-langserver"
still matches after the remap.
.Ql "dockerfile-mode" Ns No "'s"
build commands remain available via
.Ql "M-x"
(autoloaded); only font-lock changes to tree-sitter.
.It
Refreshed stale
.Ql "treesit-auto"
comments in
.Ql "init-lang-go.el"
and
.Ql "nix/mk-overlay.nix" .
Grammar set unchanged, so cache parity holds.
.El
.Pp
Curated/lite builds still fall back gracefully: a missing grammar means
.Ql "treesit-ready-p"
is nil and the classic mode stays.
